# Cloudflare Pages SPA fallback.
#
# Expo Router's web build is a single-page app: one index.html plus a JS
# bundle, with routing done in the browser. Pages serves static files, so
# without this rule a request for /today or a refresh on /goals/<id> looks for
# a file that was never emitted and returns a 404. The 200 (rather than a
# redirect) hands back index.html while keeping the URL, so the router can
# read the path and render the right screen.
#
# Anything under /_expo/ is a real emitted file and is matched before this
# catch-all, so bundles and assets are unaffected.
/*    /index.html   200
